/-!
# The window tree of the residual of the Magnus--Moldavanskii step

Target: `Work.OROneRel.magnus_residual_winTreeSplitting` -- the *tree* form of the `Z`-domain
splitting of `G = ⟨α | u ^ l⟩` over the window vertex `winVertex Wt c lo hi u l`:

  `∃ τ, cohom c τ = ofAdd 1 ∧ IsTree (GradedHNN.Coset (winVertex …) (mk τ))`.

## What is proved here (sorry-free, axiom-clean)

* `magnus_residual_winTreeSplitting_of_pair`: the tree form follows from the **sharp pair form**
  (`∃ τ` of weight one with `winVertex ⊔ zpowers (mk τ) = ⊤` and `hnnConjMap (winVertex) (mk τ)`
  injective).  This is the standard splitting form of the project
  (`Work.OROneRel.winVertexSplits`, `Work.OROneRel.magnus_residual_winSplitting_v2`), and the bridge
  is the pair of proved lemmas `Work.OROneRel.exists_split_of_cosetTree`
  (tree ⟹ generation + injectivity) and `Work.OROneRel.isTree_coset_of_hnnConjMap_injective`
  (generation + injectivity ⟹ tree).
* `magnus_residual_winTreeSplitting_of_pinData`: the tree form follows from the **pin data** of
  `Submission/Work/OROneRel/hnnSplitPin.lean` -- a family `Q : ℤ → winHd` with
  `winTheta (Q j) = mk (Wt j * (Wt 1) ^ (-j))` together with the consistency of the coedge labels --
  by composing the two lemmas proved by the fleet for this file,
  `Work.OROneRel.winHd_pinned_hnn_iso_of_pin` (pin data ⟹ pinned HNN structure for the pair
  `(winVertex, mk (Wt 1))`) and `Work.OROneRel.isTree_coset_of_pinned_hnn_iso` (pinned HNN structure
  ⟹ coset graph a tree, by Bass--Serre).

## The remaining gap (documented for the next session)

The requested theorem is *not* yet proved here; what is proved (sorry-free) is the **complete
reduction** of the target to two independent pieces, both of which are delegated:

* `magnus_residual_winTreeSplitting_of_absTree` -- the abstract Bass--Serre reduction: from
  * a tree `V` for the free group `F α` (arrow universe = vertex universe), without inversions,
  * a vertex `v` with `Stab v = (winRho Wt c lo hi).range` and an edge `v ⟶ z` with `τ • z = v`,
  * the generation `winVertex ⊔ ⟪mk τ⟫ = ⊤`,
  one gets `IsTree (Coset (winVertex …) (mk τ))`.  The argument: `u = winRho (winRoot)` lies in the
  free-group vertex, so `R = ⟨⟨u ^ l⟩⟩` is generated by elliptic elements; the Bass--Serre/JL
  lemma `isTree_orbitV_of_normalClosure_elliptic` makes the quotient `V ⧸ R` a tree; the quotient
  group `G = F α ⧸ R` acts on it without inversions (`quotient_actsWithoutInversions`), the class of
  `v` has stabiliser `(winRho.range).map mk = winVertex` (`stabilizer_quotient_mk`,
  `stabilizer_baseC_eq`), and the class of the edge is closed up by `mk τ`, so
  `hnnConjMap_injective_of_tree` yields the injectivity of `hnnConjMap (winVertex) (mk τ)`, which
  together with the generation gives the tree by `isTree_coset_of_hnnConjMap_injective`.
* `magnus_residual_winTreeSplitting_of_freeTree` -- the same from the **concrete** free-group tree
  `IsTree (GradedHNN.Coset (winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ)` (whose arrows live at universe `0`): the
  arrows are `ULift`ed (`arrowULift`, `isTree_arrowULift`, `actsWithoutInversions_arrowULift`,
  `arrowULiftGraphAction`) so that the arrow universe matches the vertex universe, as the
  Bass--Serre quotient theory requires, and the abstract reduction is applied.

So the target follows from the conjunction of

* **(P-A)** `Work.OROneRel.winRhoRange_cosetTree_window_v2` -- the free-group (`F α`, no relator)
  half of Linton's `Z`-domain splitting: the coset graph of the pair `((winRho Wt c lo hi).range, τ)`
  is a tree, for `τ` of weight one whose walk lies in the window.  This is the geometric content
  (the graph-of-spaces/nerve argument at the level of the free group);
* **(P-B)** `Work.OROneRel.winVertex_generation_exists_windowWalk_v2` -- the existence of a weight-one
  `τ` whose walk lies in the window and which generates `G` together with `winVertex`.

Both carry the *case hypotheses* of the target (`hu`, `hnd`, `hnlo`, `hnfk`, `hnc`, …), which are
precisely what excludes the counterexamples to their un-strengthened forms (the first delegation
came back refuted by data with `eps a u = 0` resp. `hnd` failing).  Once they land the target is
the two-line assembly
`obtain ⟨τ, hτ, hwalk, hgen⟩ := …; exact ⟨τ, hτ, …_of_freeTree … (…_cosetTree_window …) hgen⟩`.

Two further pieces of intelligence from the delegations (both provable independently, and now
recorded in the header of `Submission/Work/OROneRel/winRhoRange_cosetTree_window_v2.lean`):

* for a weight-one `τ` whose walk lies in the window one has `τ * (Wt 1)⁻¹ ∈ (winRho Wt c lo hi).range`,
  and the coset graph of a pair `(H, t)` depends only on the *double coset* `H t H`; hence the
  target's conclusion is **equivalent** to `IsTree (Coset (winRho Wt c lo hi).range (Wt 1))` -- the
  `τ`-quantifier (and the gauge) are harmless, and the target says exactly "the coset graph of the
  pair (window vertex, level-one tree-path gauge element) is a tree";
* (P-A) is *not* refuted by the counterexample to its un-strengthened form, but it is the missing
  chapter: in this workspace it is Linton's one-dimensional `Z`-domain splitting for the band of the
  walk (`(cdt1)`--`(cdt3)` plus the graph-of-spaces `π₁`-computation).

The previously attempted routes are *not* viable and are recorded so that they are not re-opened:
the pin/consistency route (`winPinConsistency_windowData`) is *equivalent* to
`winVertex = mk ((cohom c).ker)` (the vertex being the whole weight kernel, i.e. the normal case);
`Work.OROneRel.winVertex_eq_map_ker_cohom_v2` is FALSE; the telescoping/meet conditions are unsound
(`telescoping_britton` is FALSE, machine-checked).  The pair form of the splitting is *equivalent*
to the target, so it is not delegated.
-/

namespace Work.OROneRel

namespace Low

universe u

set_option maxHeartbeats 2000000

/-- **The tree form from the sharp pair form.**  If some deck element `τ` of weight one makes the
window vertex generate `G = ⟨α | u ^ l⟩` together with `mk τ`, and makes the canonical comparison map
`hnnConjMap (winVertex) (mk τ)` injective, then the coset graph of the pair is a tree. -/
theorem magnus_residual_winTreeSplitting_of_pair {α : Type u} [Fintype α] [DecidableEq α]
    (u : FreeGroup α) (l : ℕ) {c : α → ℤ} (Wt : ℤ → FreeGroup α) (lo hi : ℤ)
    (hpair : ∃ τ : FreeGroup α, Work.OROneRel.cohom c τ = Multiplicative.ofAdd 1 ∧
      winVertex Wt c lo hi u l ⊔
          Subgroup.zpowers (PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) τ) = ⊤ ∧
      Function.Injective (hnnConjMap (winVertex Wt c lo hi u l)
        (PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) τ))) :
    ∃ τ : FreeGroup α, Work.OROneRel.cohom c τ = Multiplicative.ofAdd 1 ∧
      Work.ORBassSerre.IsTree
        (GradedHNN.Coset (winVertex Wt c lo hi u l)
          (PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) τ)) := by
  obtain ⟨τ, hτ, hgen, hinj⟩ := hpair
  refine ⟨τ, hτ, ?_⟩
  rw [Subgroup.zpowers_eq_closure] at hgen
  exact Work.OROneRel.isTree_coset_of_hnnConjMap_injective (winVertex Wt c lo hi u l)
    (PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) τ) hgen hinj

/-- **The tree form from the pin data.**

Given the pin and consistency of `Submission/Work/OROneRel/hnnSplitPin.lean` -- a family
`Q : ℤ → winHd` with `winTheta (Q j) = mk (Wt j * (Wt 1) ^ (-j))` and the level-independence of the
conjugated coedge labels -- the pair `(winVertex, mk (Wt 1))` carries a pinned HNN structure
(`Work.OROneRel.winHd_pinned_hnn_iso_of_pin`), whence -- by Bass--Serre
(`Work.OROneRel.isTree_coset_of_pinned_hnn_iso`) -- the coset graph is a tree.  This wires the two
proved pieces of the pair-form route together; the *gap* is exactly the production of this pin data
from the hypotheses of the residual (see the module docstring). -/
theorem magnus_residual_winTreeSplitting_of_pinData {α : Type u} [Fintype α] [DecidableEq α]
    (u : FreeGroup α) (l : ℕ) (hl : 1 ≤ l) {c : α → ℤ} (hcu : Work.OROneRel.cohom c u = 1)
    {Wt : ℤ → FreeGroup α} {lo hi : ℤ} (hW0 : Wt 0 = 1)
    (hcoh : ∀ i : ℤ, Work.OROneRel.cohom c (Wt i) = Multiplicative.ofAdd i)
    (hwin : ∀ p ∈ Work.OROneRel.decor c 0 (Work.OROneRel.wordOf u),
      Work.OROneRel.coverEdge p ∈ Work.OROneRel.winE c lo hi)
    (htree : ∀ i : ℤ, lo ≤ i → i ≤ hi →
      ∀ q ∈ Work.OROneRel.decor c 0 (Work.OROneRel.wordOf (Wt i)),
        Work.OROneRel.coverEdge q ∈ Work.OROneRel.winTree Wt c lo hi)
    (hcov : ∀ x : α, ∃ i : ℤ, (x, i) ∈ Work.OROneRel.winE c lo hi)
    (hlo1 : lo ≤ 1) (hhi1 : 1 ≤ hi)
    (hA : ∀ x : FreeGroup (Work.OROneRel.winBeta Wt c lo hi),
      Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi x ∈
          Subgroup.normalClosure ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) →
        x ∈ Subgroup.normalClosure
          ({Work.OROneRel.winRoot Wt c lo hi u ^ l} :
            Set (FreeGroup (Work.OROneRel.winBeta Wt c lo hi))))
    {A : Subgroup (Work.OROneRel.winHd Wt c lo hi u l)} {ψ : A ≃* A}
    (hψ : ∀ a : A, PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) (Wt 1) *
        Work.OROneRel.winTheta Wt c lo hi u l hW0 hcu hwin
          (a : Work.OROneRel.winHd Wt c lo hi u l) =
      Work.OROneRel.winTheta Wt c lo hi u l hW0 hcu hwin
          (ψ a : Work.OROneRel.winHd Wt c lo hi u l) *
        PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) (Wt 1))
    {Q : ℤ → Work.OROneRel.winHd Wt c lo hi u l}
    (hQ : ∀ j : ℤ, Work.OROneRel.winTheta Wt c lo hi u l hW0 hcu hwin (Q j) =
      PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) (Wt j * (Wt 1) ^ (-j)))
    (hcons : ∀ (x : α) (i j : ℤ), (x, i) ∈ Work.OROneRel.winE c lo hi →
      (x, j) ∈ Work.OROneRel.winE c lo hi →
      (Work.OROneRel.levelEl (A := A) (ψ := ψ) Q i)⁻¹ *
          Work.OROneRel.winGammaK Wt c lo hi u l A ψ (x, i) *
          Work.OROneRel.levelEl (A := A) (ψ := ψ) Q (i + c x) =
        (Work.OROneRel.levelEl (A := A) (ψ := ψ) Q j)⁻¹ *
          Work.OROneRel.winGammaK Wt c lo hi u l A ψ (x, j) *
          Work.OROneRel.levelEl (A := A) (ψ := ψ) Q (j + c x)) :
    ∃ τ : FreeGroup α, Work.OROneRel.cohom c τ = Multiplicative.ofAdd 1 ∧
      Work.ORBassSerre.IsTree
        (GradedHNN.Coset (winVertex Wt c lo hi u l)
          (PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) τ)) := by
  have hθ : Function.Injective (Work.OROneRel.winTheta Wt c lo hi u l hW0 hcu hwin) :=
    Work.OROneRel.winTheta_injective_of_freiheitssatz u l hW0 hcu hwin hA
  obtain ⟨A', B', φ', e, he_of, he_t⟩ :=
    Work.OROneRel.winHd_pinned_hnn_iso_of_pin u l hl hcu hW0 hcoh hwin htree hcov hlo1 hhi1
      hθ hψ hQ hcons
  exact ⟨Wt 1, hcoh 1,
    Work.OROneRel.isTree_coset_of_pinned_hnn_iso (winVertex Wt c lo hi u l)
      (PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) (Wt 1)) A' B' φ' e he_of he_t⟩

/-- **The tree form from a tree for the *free* level-group (abstract form).**

If the free group `F α` acts on a tree `V` (with the arrow universe of `V` equal to its vertex
universe, as required by the Bass--Serre quotient theory), without inversions, with a vertex `v`
whose stabiliser is the free-group window vertex `P = (winRho Wt c lo hi).range`, and with an edge
`e : v ⟶ z` such that `τ • z = v`, then -- together with the generation
`winVertex ⊔ ⟪mk τ⟫ = ⊤` -- the coset graph of the pair `(winVertex, mk τ)` is a tree.

The proof is the Bass--Serre/JL argument: `u ^ l` is elliptic (`u = winRho (winRoot)`), so
`R = ⟨⟨u ^ l⟩⟩` is generated by elliptic elements, whence the quotient graph `V ⧸ R` is a tree
(`isTree_orbitV_of_normalClosure_elliptic`); the quotient group `G = F α ⧸ R` acts on it without
inversions (`quotient_actsWithoutInversions`), the class of `v` has stabiliser
`(winRho.range).map mk = winVertex`, and the class of the edge is closed up by `mk τ`, so
`hnnConjMap_injective_of_tree` gives the injectivity of `hnnConjMap (winVertex) (mk τ)`, which
together with the generation gives the tree by `isTree_coset_of_hnnConjMap_injective`. -/
theorem magnus_residual_winTreeSplitting_of_absTree {α : Type u} [Fintype α] [DecidableEq α]
    (u : FreeGroup α) (l : ℕ)
    {c : α → ℤ} (hcu : Work.OROneRel.cohom c u = 1)
    {Wt : ℤ → FreeGroup α} {lo hi : ℤ} (hW0 : Wt 0 = 1)
    (hwin : ∀ p ∈ Work.OROneRel.decor c 0 (Work.OROneRel.wordOf u),
      Work.OROneRel.coverEdge p ∈ Work.OROneRel.winE c lo hi)
    {τ : FreeGroup α} (hτ : Work.OROneRel.cohom c τ = Multiplicative.ofAdd 1)
    {V : Type u} [Quiver.{u, u} V] [Quiver.HasInvolutiveReverse V]
    [MulAction (FreeGroup α) V] [Work.ORBassSerre.GraphAction (FreeGroup α) V]
    (hT : Work.ORBassSerre.IsTree V)
    (hninv : Work.ORBassSerre.ActsWithoutInversions (FreeGroup α) V)
    (v : V) {z : V} (e : v ⟶ z)
    (hstab : MulAction.stabilizer (FreeGroup α) v = (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range)
    (hclose : τ • z = v)
    (hgen : winVertex Wt c lo hi u l ⊔
      Subgroup.zpowers (PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) τ) = ⊤) :
    Work.ORBassSerre.IsTree
      (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.Coset (winVertex Wt c lo hi u l)
        (PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) τ)) := by
  classical
  have huP : u ∈ (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range :=
    ⟨Work.OROneRel.winRoot Wt c lo hi u,
      Work.OROneRel.winRho_winRoot Wt hW0 hcu lo hi hwin⟩
  have hfix : ∀ g ∈ ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)), ∃ w : V, g • w = w := by
    intro g hg
    rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hg
    subst hg
    refine ⟨v, ?_⟩
    rw [← MulAction.mem_stabilizer_iff, hstab]
    exact Subgroup.pow_mem _ huP l
  have hQ : Work.ORBassSerre.IsTree
      (Work.ORBassSerre.orbitV (↥(Subgroup.normalClosure ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)))) V) :=
    Work.ORBassSerre.Action.isTree_orbitV_of_normalClosure_elliptic hT
      (Subgroup.normalClosure ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α))) ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) hfix rfl
  have hninv' : Work.ORBassSerre.ActsWithoutInversions
      (FreeGroup α ⧸ Subgroup.normalClosure ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)))
      (Work.ORBassSerre.orbitV (↥(Subgroup.normalClosure ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)))) V) :=
    Work.ORDunwoody.quotient_actsWithoutInversions hninv
      (Subgroup.normalClosure ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)))
  have hstab' : MulAction.stabilizer
      (FreeGroup α ⧸ Subgroup.normalClosure ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)))
      (Quotient.mk'' v : Work.ORBassSerre.orbitV
        (↥(Subgroup.normalClosure ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)))) V)
      = winVertex Wt c lo hi u l := by
    rw [Work.ORBassSerre.QuotientTree.stabilizer_quotient_mk, hstab]
    rfl
  have hclose' : (QuotientGroup.mk' (Subgroup.normalClosure ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)))) τ •
      (Quotient.mk'' z : Work.ORBassSerre.orbitV
        (↥(Subgroup.normalClosure ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)))) V)
      = (Quotient.mk'' v : Work.ORBassSerre.orbitV
        (↥(Subgroup.normalClosure ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)))) V) := by
    rw [Work.ORBassSerre.quotient_smul_mk, hclose]
  have hinj : Function.Injective
      (Work.OROneRel.hnnConjMap (winVertex Wt c lo hi u l)
        (PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) τ)) := by
    have h := Work.OROneRel.hnnConjMap_injective_of_tree hQ hninv'
      (Quotient.mk'' v : Work.ORBassSerre.orbitV
        (↥(Subgroup.normalClosure ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)))) V)
      ((QuotientGroup.mk' (Subgroup.normalClosure ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)))) τ)
      (Work.ORBassSerre.orbitArrow (G := ↥(Subgroup.normalClosure
        ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)))) e) hclose'
    rwa [hstab'] at h
  rw [Subgroup.zpowers_eq_closure] at hgen
  exact Work.OROneRel.isTree_coset_of_hnnConjMap_injective (winVertex Wt c lo hi u l)
    (PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) τ) hgen hinj

/-- **The tree form from a tree for the *free* level-group.**  The `F α`-tree of the free-group
splitting is here given in its concrete form, `IsTree (GradedHNN.Coset (winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ)`
-- this is the conclusion of `Work.OROneRel.winRhoRange_cosetTree_window`, the geometric half of
Linton's `Z`-domain splitting at the level of the free group.  The arrow universe of that coset
graph is `0`, while the Bass--Serre quotient theory requires the arrow universe to be the vertex
universe, so the arrows are `ULift`ed (`Work.OROneRel.arrowULift`) before the abstract reduction
`magnus_residual_winTreeSplitting_of_absTree` is applied. -/
theorem magnus_residual_winTreeSplitting_of_freeTree {α : Type u} [Fintype α] [DecidableEq α]
    (u : FreeGroup α) (l : ℕ)
    {c : α → ℤ} (hcu : Work.OROneRel.cohom c u = 1)
    {Wt : ℤ → FreeGroup α} {lo hi : ℤ} (hW0 : Wt 0 = 1)
    (hcoh : ∀ i : ℤ, Work.OROneRel.cohom c (Wt i) = Multiplicative.ofAdd i)
    (hwin : ∀ p ∈ Work.OROneRel.decor c 0 (Work.OROneRel.wordOf u),
      Work.OROneRel.coverEdge p ∈ Work.OROneRel.winE c lo hi)
    {τ : FreeGroup α} (hτ : Work.OROneRel.cohom c τ = Multiplicative.ofAdd 1)
    (hTree₀ : Work.ORBassSerre.IsTree
      (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.Coset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ))
    (hgen : winVertex Wt c lo hi u l ⊔
      Subgroup.zpowers (PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) τ) = ⊤) :
    Work.ORBassSerre.IsTree
      (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.Coset (winVertex Wt c lo hi u l)
        (PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) τ)) := by
  classical
  -- the arrow-`ULift` of the free-group coset graph
  have hlift : @Work.ORBassSerre.IsTree
      (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.Coset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ)
      (Work.OROneRel.arrowULiftQuiver _
        (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.instQuiverCoset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ))
      (Work.OROneRel.arrowULiftHasInvolutiveReverse _
        (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.instQuiverCoset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ)
        (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.instHasInvolutiveReverseCoset
          (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ)) :=
    Work.OROneRel.isTree_arrowULift
      (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.instHasInvolutiveReverseCoset
        (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ) hTree₀
  -- the transported graph action and no-inversions
  have hninv₀ : @Work.ORBassSerre.ActsWithoutInversions (FreeGroup α)
      (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.Coset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ) _
      (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.instQuiverCoset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ)
      (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.instHasReverseCoset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ)
      (MulAction.quotient (FreeGroup α) (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range)
      (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.instGraphActionCoset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ) :=
    Work.OROneRel.actsWithoutInversions_coset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ
      (Work.OROneRel.cohom c)
      (fun h => Work.OROneRel.cohom_eq_one_of_mem_winRho_range Wt c lo hi hcoh h.2) hτ
  have hninv₁ := Work.OROneRel.actsWithoutInversions_arrowULift
    (Q := Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.instQuiverCoset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ)
    (M := MulAction.quotient (FreeGroup α) (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range)
    (HR := Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.instHasReverseCoset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ)
    (GA := Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.instGraphActionCoset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ)
    hninv₀
  -- assemble: the abstract reduction applied to the lifted tree
  letI hQ : Quiver.{u, u}
      (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.Coset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ) :=
    Work.OROneRel.arrowULiftQuiver _
      (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.instQuiverCoset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ)
  letI hR : Quiver.HasInvolutiveReverse
      (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.Coset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ) :=
    Work.OROneRel.arrowULiftHasInvolutiveReverse _
      (Work.OROneRel.GradedHNN.instQuiverCoset (Work.OROneRel.winRho Wt c lo hi).range τ)
